# The SHA-1 of the certificate every macOS release binary must be signed with.
# Read by scripts/lib/mac-signing.sh (mac_pinned_sha1): '#' comments and blank
# lines are ignored, and what remains must be empty or exactly one 40-hex-digit
# fingerprint (colons, spaces and case do not matter).
#
# BOOTSTRAP: no fingerprint below yet. The identity has not been provisioned,
# so the mac leg signs AD-HOC (hardened runtime + the entitlements, no
# certificate) and warns loudly; OAM_SIGN_REQUIRED=1 refuses that instead.
# Once a fingerprint is committed here, signing with exactly that certificate
# is mandatory: a mac leg that cannot use it fails the release.
#
# To fill it in: on the build Mac run
#     bash scripts/provision-mac-signing.sh --generate
# back up oam-codesign.p12 + oam-codesign.p12-password off that host, and put
# the printed sha1 on its own line below, in the same commit that says so.
# Rotating it (a new identity, or the Developer ID) is the same edit.
